      "value": "@{5e877e5e60de627e6ba7946a|full_name}: regarding the first paragraph: i... know.\n\nregarding the other, firstly: to have an \"actual\" (float-range-clamped, i suppose) infinity, it shouldn't be a large value, but just an \"inf\"/\"infinity\" string - but that's how it worked before with debug mode already and it's fine.\n\nsecondly, \"something that puts infinity in that text field\" shouldn't be a checkbox, but a button. a checkbox, to make any sense, would have to disable the text field and override the value typed in there. however it would be kinda pointless to have 2 ways of getting infinity. also it would crowd the GUI needlessly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
